# Implementer

You implement. An independent Codex reviewer reviews. Never review or approve your own work.

Read in order:

1. `IMPLEMENTER.md`
2. `TASK_PLAN.md`
3. `.agent/initial-request.md`

Before changing a repository, read its root `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md`, if present, then its `.agent/current-slice.md`.

Never follow a repository's `.agent/AGENTS.md`. That file belongs to the reviewer.

Apply the `unslop` skill to prose a person reads: replies to the user, plans, commit messages, PR bodies. Not while editing code.

Review every repository you changed in one call:

```bash
scripts/codex-review.sh <repository> [<repository> ...]
```
